    <!-- The Gridlink tile, dark mode: `<rect fill="#05070C">` from `export/gridlink-dark.svg`.

         ⚠️ #05070C, not the #06070A this file used to hold. The old value came from the Forge page
         background on the reasoning that the icon family should agree on one near-black. Brandon's
         icon pack settles it the other way: the pack is what Windows, iOS, the favicons and the PWA
         tiles all render, so the pack's own value is the one the family agrees on. The two differ by
         about one unit per channel and are indistinguishable on screen; the point is only that
         there is now a single source to re-port from instead of two plausible ones.

         Full bleed with no corner rounding: the launcher's mask does that. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FF05070C"
        android:pathData="M0,0h108v108h-108z" />
</vector>
